rem Perfect Square Collection
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=142
rem Find the least x + y + z, x > y > z,
rem with x +- y, x +- z and y +- z all
rem perfect squares

use sequences
use io
use cli

option Top integer = 1100

rem Let x + y = a^2, x + z = c^2 and
rem x - z = d^2. Then y - z = a^2 - c^2,
rem y + z = a^2 - d^2 and x - y =
rem c^2 + d^2 - a^2 must be squares too.
rem Keep pairs (a, c) whose a^2 - c^2 is
rem a square, pair each with every d of
rem the parity of c, and test the other
rem two differences.
Root = 0 to Top array
Cap = Top * Top
Sq = array shape (Cap + 1) fill 0
Sq (Root * Root) = 1
Side = 2 to Top array
Rows = Side len
A = Side reshape Rows 1
C = Side reshape 1 Rows
Gap = (A * A - C * C) 0 max
Pairs = Rows * Rows
Flat = Gap reshape Pairs
Ok = (Sq Flat equal 1) reshape Rows Rows
Ok and= C less A
Pos = Ok indices
Pa = Side (Pos # 0)
Pc = Side (Pos # 1)
Cnt = Pa len
D = (1 to Top array) reshape 1 Top
A2 = (Pa * Pa) reshape Cnt 1
C2 = (Pc * Pc) reshape Cnt 1
D2 = D * D
Cc = Pc reshape Cnt 1
Low = C2 + D2 - A2
Fit = D less Cc
Fit and= (C2 - D2) mod 2 equal 0
Fit and= Low greater 0
Cells = Cnt * Top
Lo1 = Low 0 max
Hi1 = (Lo1 reshape Cells) Cap min
Sq1 = (Sq Hi1) reshape Cnt Top
Lo2 = (A2 - D2) 0 max
Hi2 = (Lo2 reshape Cells) Cap min
Sq2 = (Sq Hi2) reshape Cnt Top
Hit = Fit and Sq1 equal 1
Hit and= Sq2 equal 1
Total = A2 + (C2 - D2) // 2
Sums = Total filter Hit array
Best = concat Sums (array 2 * Cap)
Answer = Best min
Answer print
